title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The DDP cannot govern by itself yet. Because we dont have a electoral majority, we need to get the support of the other parties to let us into their coalitions and collaborate, in government or in opposition.

- @dvp: Strengthen our bonds with the <span style="color: #C0A054;">conservative-liberal</span> DVP.
- @center: Contact sympathetic members of the Z who wish to continue our <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> coalition.
- @spd: Strengthen our bonds with the SPD, longtime allies of our party and our predecessors.
- @dnvp: Contact the DNVP where necessary.
- @bourgeois: Strengthen our bonds with smaller bourgeois parties.
- @ddp_alone: The DDP can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@spd
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; spd_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)
go-to: spd_op if spd_in_government = 1 and ddp_in_government = 0; spd_coalition if spd_in_government = 1 and ddp_in_government = 1; ddp_op if spd_in_government = 0 and ddp_in_government = 1

@spd_op
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the SPD-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@spd_coalition
on-arrival: spd_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@ddp_op
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We hold government without them at present, but the SPD remains a natural partner should the coalition math shift.


@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; z_relation += 7*(1 - dissent)

The Z has been a natural ally and with the newly founded state, we should be able to continue the <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> Coalition.


@dvp
subtitle: -1 resources </br> The dream of <span style="color: #C0A054;">lib</span><span style="color: #DCCA4A;">eral</span> unity.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; dvp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); dvp_left += 1
go-to: dvp_op if ddp_in_government = 1 and dvp_in_government = 0;

Many of our members originate from the DVP, and we have contacts within them.


@dvp_op
on-arrival: dvp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

They are currently in opposition to our government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@dnvp
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; dnvp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The DNVP are a half-time coalition partner with us, and most members of our party are uncomfortable at the thought of establishing even more contact with them, but if that is what it takes to get into government..

@bourgeois
subtitle: -1 resources
view-if: dbp_exist or csvd_exist or wp_exist or cnblp_exist
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; dbp_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); csvd_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); wp_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); cnblp_relation += 4*(1 - dissent)

We have improved our relations with some smaller bourgeois parties.


@ddp_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
